      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "•A versatile mixed-use property combining a three-bedroom detached residence with adjoining commercial premises.\n•Established commercial premises currently operating as a successful florist, with potential for a variety of alternative uses.\n•Well-proportioned residential accommodation comprising an entrance hallway, living room, kitchen/dining area, family bathroom, and three bedrooms.\n•The property benefits from a generous front site and gated side access, offering excellent flexibility for a range of uses\n\n\nDescription\n\nAn excellent opportunity to acquire a well-presented three-bedroom detached residence together with a substantial single-storey commercial premises, ideally suited to a variety of business uses.\n\nThe residential accommodation is complemented by a generous commercial unit currently laid out as a florist, together with extensive tarmac parking to the front, rear garden/yard space and excellent side access.\n\nLocation\n\nSituated adjacent to the Athy distributor road, Fortbarrington Road is ideally positioned within easy reach of Athy town and its excellent range of local amenities. The property also benefits from convenient access to the M9 (via N78), with the nearby towns of Kildare, Newbridge and Naas all within easy reach. Athy is a picturesque market town set at the meeting point of the Grand Canal and River Barrow. Rich in history and surrounded by attractive countryside, the town offers a relaxed setting with a strong sense of community and an excellent range of local amenities. The weekly farmers` market, historic landmarks and scenic green spaces add to its appeal.\n\nThe town caters well for families and active lifestyles, with a selection of schools, sporting clubs and recreational facilities available locally. Athy also benefits from excellent transport connections, with convenient access to the M7 and M9 motorways, regular bus services and the Dublin Waterford railway line. Rail services provide a direct connection to Dublin Heuston, with journey times of under 45 minutes.\n\n\nGuide Price\n\nIn excess of 595,000\n\nType of Transaction\n\nPrivate Treaty\n\nAccommodation:\n\nResidential Premises \n\nDriveway\nCobble lock driveway and side entrance with wooden gate.\n\nEntrance Hallway 3.95m x 1.8m \nOak parquet flooring, coving, open space under stairway\n\nLiving Room 4.25m x 3.95m\nOak parquet flooring, decorative coving and open fireplace, with two windows\n\nKitchen / Dining Room 6.2m x 3.33m\nTiled flooring, light fitting, shaker style floor to wall solid wood kitchen cabinets, induction hob, double oven, extractor fan, stainless steel sink, fully plumbed with washing machine, dishwasher, free standing fridge/freezer, tiled splashback and door that leading to rear garden.\n\nBedroom 1 3.19m x 4,1m\nCarpeted Floor, dual windows\n\n\nBedroom 2 4.07m x 2.44m\nCarpeted Floor, fitted wardrobes\n\nBedroom 3 3.97m x 3.03m\nCarpeted Floor, fitted wardrobes, vanity unit\n\nBathroom 1.96m x 2.46m\nWooden floor, power shower, vanity unit, w.c. and w.h.b. \n\n\nCommercial Premises \n\nRetail Space 12.13m x 7.13m\n\nTiled floor, air conditioning, rear access \n\nRear Yard\n\nTarmac surface, independent side access, lean to and large shed.\n\nAdditional Information:\n\n•Commercial unit currently operating as a florist\n•Site totalling approx. 0.15 hectares (approx. 0.38 acres)\n•Extensive parking area to front\n•Large rear yard/garden to commercial premises with a varied selection of sheds and storage\n•Built c.1990\n•Air conditioning to commercial unit\n•Excellent opportunity for owner-occupier or investor\n•Retail gross internal floor area of approx. 82 sq.m. (880 sq.ft)\n•Residential gross internal floor area of approx. 91 sq.m. (980 sq.ft)\n\nItems Included in sale:\nThe residential property is being sold as seen with furniture, appliances and light fittings to be included in the sale.\n\nServices\nMains electricity and water, oil fired central heating \n\nBER \nResidential - C\nRetail - C3\n\nViewing\n\nBy appointment only.\n\nDirections:\n\nEircode: R14 DE93\n\nContact Information\n\nMorgan Graham\nE: morgang@coonan.com\nT: +353 45 832020\n\n\n"
      },
